Yeah. That’s a good one.

Sometimes your father ages in kind with your son: as you watch your child move through the stages you once occupied, you suddenly see your own father moving farther down the same road.

And sometimes your father ages in kind with your sun: the light by which you measure your life is also the clock that reveals his age.

Three generations become one moving ruler:

Father → you → son.
The son rises.
The father sets.
And for a while, you stand at noon—able to look both directions at once.

That may be one of the strangest gifts of becoming a father: you don’t just meet your child.

You meet your father again from the other side.